The [[Pandamonium]] is a neutral [[Weapon]] normally obtained by combining a [[Pan]] with a [[Corrupted Crystal]]. Compared to the [[Pan]], it uses substantially less stamina and deals a similar amount of damage on its own as a [[Pan]] with four or five [[Food]]s around it. In addition, the [[Pandamonium]] inflicts 1 {{icon/poison}} for each {{icon/star}} [[Food]] activation, and gives {{icon/poison}} a chance of critical hit per {{icon/star}} [[Food]]. Between these two abilities, there's a lot of additional damage possible, especially with other sources of {{icon/poison}}.

There are 13 {{icon/star}} slots, so the maximum {{icon/poison}} crit chance is 52%, but the {{icon/star}} slots are tightly spaced, so this would require at least five 1-tile [[Food]]s for the innermost spaces.

== Description ==
''Prophecy says it brings chaos through the means of food poisoning.''

== Trivia ==
[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pand%C3%A6monium_(Paradise_Lost) Pandæmonium] is the capital of Hell in John Milton's epic poem ''Paradise Lost''.  

